  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently we don't fire a load event when we restore a page from BFCache. This introduces behavior where a page that has not yet been completely loaded, but deemed eligible for BFCache when navigating away, upon restore does not fire a load event when it completes.\n\nChrome specifically has this behavior. I don't know what Safari does and Firefox is expanding its capabilities for BFCache eligibility, but probably will not allow pages to be put into bfcache if not completely loaded.\n\nIt's unclear if BFCache eligibility hinges on a load event having been fired, but if it doesn't, not firing a `load` event upon restore doesn't seem like sound behavior either.",
